    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/GreyBlight_Disease -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/GreyBlight_Disease">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/Disease"/>
        <favoredByCondition rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/HighHumidity_Instance"/>
        <favoredByCondition rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/HighTemperature_Instance"/>
        <favoredByCondition rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/LeafWetnessLong_Instance"/>
        <favoredByCondition rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/PlantStress_Instance"/>
        <favoredByCondition rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/PoorAirCirculation_Instance"/>
        <favoredBySymptom rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/BlackFruitingBodyDots_Instance"/>
        <favoredBySymptom rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/ConcentricRingPatch_Instance"/>
        <favoredBySymptom rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/GreySilveredCenter_Instance"/>
        <hasTreatment rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/GreyBlight_Treatment_01"/>
        <hasTreatment rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/GreyBlight_Treatment_02"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Dull brown spot expands into a circular to irregular patch, often with faint concentric zoning; centre fades to pale grey or silvered tone inside a darker brown border; minute black fruiting bodies appear as dots. Wound-dependent fungus — favoured by warm, humid conditions with poor air movement and long leaf wetness, but far more serious on debilitated bushes (drought stress, sunscorch, waterlogging, unbalanced nutrition, pest damage aftermath) than on vigorous ones. Attacks via wounds rather than tender leaf directly, unlike Blister Blight.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/GreyBlight_Treatment_01 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/GreyBlight_Treatment_01">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/Treatment"/>
        <stepOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</stepOrder>
        <treatmentText>No special control measures are recommended for grey blight, a minor leaf disease in Sri Lanka. Regular copper sprays applied against blister blight prevent it from becoming a problem.</treatmentText>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: Handbook on Tea, ch. 14 (Common Diseases of Tea and their Management), Control section on minor leaf diseases</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/GreyBlight_Treatment_02 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/GreyBlight_Treatment_02">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/Treatment"/>
        <stepOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</stepOrder>
        <treatmentText>Occasional outbreaks in heavy mist pockets can be brought under control with the usual copper fungicide sprays.</treatmentText>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: Handbook on Tea, ch. 14 (Common Diseases of Tea and their Management), Control section on minor leaf diseases</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


